WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:06.900
In 1970, trade between countries was
worth 25.8 per cent of world GDP.

2
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:11.280
By 2008, it had climbed to 60.3 per cent.

3
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.310
Trade was growing much faster than output.

4
00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:17.340
Container ships, cheap
calls across continents,

5
00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:21.060
and one product made in
stages in several countries.

6
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.210
So why did the world start
trading so much more,

7
00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.600
and does everyone come out ahead?

8
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.610
In this mission, you'll
read decades of trade data

9
00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:33.130
and uncover what a more
open world brings a country.

10
00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:36.320
Then you'll weigh those gains
against the industries and jobs

11
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.980
that come under pressure.

12
00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:41.990
Your mission: find out who gains
from a more connected world,

13
00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:43.080
and who pays.
